### Multi-Platform Conditional Compilation with Unity Directives (C#)

Source: https://docs.unity3d.com/Manual/platform-dependent-compilation.html

This example shows how to use `#if`, `#elif`, and `#else` directives in C# to handle conditional compilation for different platforms. It checks for the `UNITY_EDITOR` symbol first, then `UNITY_IOS`, and finally logs a general message for any other platform. This allows for platform-specific logic within the same script.

```csharp
#if UNITY_EDITOR

    Debug.Log("Unity Editor");

#elif UNITY_IOS

    Debug.Log("Unity iOS");

#else

    Debug.Log("Any other platform");

#endif
```

